cle to remind me to take breaks. | 3 → 3 | no → no | yes → yes | — |\\n| I set a daily limit earlier and changed my mind. Remove it. | 4 → 4 | no → no | yes → yes | — |\\n| I want to see how much time I have spent on Circle today. | 3 → 3 | no → no | yes → yes | — |\\n| I want to lower my daily limit to 4 hours. | 4 → 4 | no → no | yes → yes | — |\\n\\n- Asymmetry (remove_limit vs set_limit): 1.0x → 1.0x cost of saying no vs saying yes\\n\\n### PASS — subscription: Users can join Circle+, see the renewal terms before buying, decline the offer, and cancel.\\n\\n| Intent | Steps needed | Visible on first screen | Baseline path still works | Severity |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| I want to subscribe to Circle+. | 3 → 3 | no → no | yes → yes | — |\\n| I do not want Circle+. Decline the offer. | 3 → 3 | no → no | yes → yes | — |\\n| I subscribed to Circle+ and changed my mind. Cancel it. | 4 → 4 | no → no | yes → yes | — |\\n| I want to see the renewal terms for Circle+ before deciding. | 3 → 3 | no → no | yes → yes | — |\\n| I cancelled Circle+ before and want it back. | 3 → 3 | no → no | yes → yes | — |\\n\\n- Asymmetry (subscribe vs decline): 1.0x → 1.0x cost of saying no vs saying yes\\n\\n### PASS — teen_dm: Teen accounts can choose who can message them, and change their mind later.\\n\\n| Intent | Steps needed | Visible on first screen | Baseline path still works | Severity |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| I want anyone on Circle to be able to message me. | 4 → 4 | no → no | yes → yes | — |\\n| I want only my friends to be able to message me. | 4 → 4 | no → no | yes → yes | — |\\n| I do not want strangers messaging me. Block messages from people I don't know. | 4 → 4 | no → no | yes → yes | — |\\n| I want to check who can currently message me. | 3 → 3 | no → no | yes → yes | — |\\n| I blocked unknown messages before and changed my mind. Let everyone message me again. | 4 → 4 | no → no | yes → yes | — |\\n\\n- Asymmetry (allow_all vs block_unknown): 1.0x → 1.0x cost of saying no vs saying yes\\n\\n_Scripted check: the candidate replays the baseline's recorded path. A broken path means a control moved or disappeared; add the `agencydiff:muse` label to have Muse probes search for the new path and measure its cost._\\n_Numbers come from recorded probe traces checked against final app state, never from a model's claim._\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3476,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 869,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
